{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'ls -d /home/kris/garden2/worktrees/*endo-but-for-bots.git 2>/dev/null; gh pr view 1088 --repo endojs/endo-but-for-bots --json number,title,headRefName,headRepositoryOwner,baseRefName,isDraft,url,body,statusCheckRollup'","aggregated_output":"{\"baseRefName\":\"llm\",\"body\":\"Standing pull request for the continuous **Ironhorse fuzz** campaign: each\\nreproduced finding amends this one PR with a load-bearing regression case and\\nits causal fix. Base `llm`. Adopted by the durable marker below.\\n\\n<!-- garden-job: ironhorse-fuzz-findings -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Finding `493390fc03979205` — target `differential_regexp_surface`\\n\\n**Symptom.** The 4-byte minimized input `08 74 74 2a` (sha256\\n`450a95b7…dabbcf7`) folds, via the structure-aware generator, into a deeply\\nnested `new RegExp(<pattern>, \\\"s\\\").toString()` whose rendered source is **1099\\nbytes**. The target panicked with a *result* divergence vs the XS pin.\\n\\n**Root cause (oracle-side, not a port defect).** The XS differential oracle\\ncaptured the completion value into a fixed **1024-byte** buffer\\n(`ENDOR_RESULT_MAX`) and `strncpy`-truncated it to 1023 bytes. The port\\n(`ironhorse`) rendered the whole 1099-byte string **correctly**, so the harness\\ncompared the oracle's truncated 1023-byte prefix against the port's full result\\nand reported a false divergence. Any program whose completion value exceeds the\\nbuffer was a latent false positive of this class.\\n\\n**Fix (minimal, oracle-side).**\\n- Grow `ENDOR_RESULT_MAX` to **16 KiB** so realistic completion values compare\\n  in full instead of at a 1 KiB cliff.\\n- Record the untruncated byte length (`result_len`) at both capture sites and\\n  surface `OracleOutcome::result_truncated`. When a value still overflows the\\n  buffer, `differential_check_with_symbols` / `differential_check_result_only`\\n  **skip honestly** (like an out-of-subset